# 📊 Alteryx Sales Data Analysis

![Alteryx](https://img.shields.io/badge/Alteryx-Data_Analytics-0078C8?logo=alteryx&logoColor=white)
![Data Preparation](https://img.shields.io/badge/Data_Preparation-ETL-blue)
![Analytics](https://img.shields.io/badge/Analytics-Sales_Analysis-purple)
![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/Status-Completed-success)

An end-to-end retail sales analytics project using **Alteryx Designer** to consolidate, clean, transform, and analyze customer and order data to uncover profitability trends and generate actionable business insights.

This project applies Alteryx's data preparation, blending, transformation, and aggregation capabilities to automate a multi-source sales analysis workflow for DC Industries, a fictional retail department store operating across three US regions.

---

## 🎯 Project Objective

The objective of this project is to develop an automated Alteryx workflow that integrates customer and order datasets, prepares them for analysis, and evaluates sales profitability across different business dimensions.

The analysis aims to:

- Identify the 25 most profitable orders.
- Determine the most profitable day of the week.
- Analyze profitability across product categories and regions.
- Identify the subcategories contributing the most profit within each category.
- Generate a consolidated dataset for external visualization and reporting.

---

## 💼 Business Problem

DC Industries needs to consolidate customer and order information stored across multiple datasets to better understand its sales performance and profitability.

Without a standardized data preparation process, analyzing information across different regions, orders, and product categories can become time-consuming and difficult to maintain.

This project addresses the problem by building a structured Alteryx workflow that automates data integration, cleansing, transformation, and aggregation, enabling more efficient sales analysis and business reporting.

---

## 📂 Dataset

The project uses four source datasets provided as part of the DataCamp case study:

| Dataset | Description |
|---|---|
| Customer Orders - West | Customer order information from the Western region |
| Customer Orders - East | Customer order information from the Eastern region |
| Regions | State-to-region mapping information |
| Order Details | Order-level product, quantity, price, cost, and payment information |

The datasets are combined to create a consolidated sales dataset containing customer, order, regional, and profitability information.

---

## 🛠 Tools Used

- Alteryx Designer
- Microsoft Excel
- CSV Data Sources
- Alteryx Workflow Automation

---

## 🔄 Project Workflow

### 1. Data Preparation and Integration

- Imported customer order datasets from the Eastern and Western regions.
- Combined datasets using the Union tool.
- Identified and removed duplicate records.
- Joined customer data with regional mapping information.
- Created a lookup table to standardize regional classifications.
- Converted order dates into a valid date format.
- Extracted the day of the week from order dates.

### 2. Data Transformation and Cleansing

- Transposed payment method fields into a structured format.
- Configured data fields and standardized column structures.
- Removed records with missing quantity values.
- Parsed product category and subcategory information.
- Calculated order profitability using price, cost, and quantity.

### 3. Sales and Profitability Analysis

Conducted aggregations and sorting to address the following business questions:

- Top 25 most profitable orders.
- Profitability by day of the week.
- Profitability by product category and region.
- Most profitable subcategories within each category.

### 4. Reporting and Data Export

- Generated regional order counts by day of the week.
- Prepared an Excel report for regional managers.
- Exported consolidated datasets for downstream visualization and reporting.
- Organized the workflow using annotations and tool containers.

